  "summary_en": "Japan's Ministerial Ordinance on Industrial Safety and Health (1972, revision in force 1 Oct 2026). It sets workplace safety management structures, risk assessment, machinery safety standards, special education and licensing. Includes provisions on industrial robots (special training for teaching and maintenance within the operating range) and industrial vehicles such as forklifts. No AI-specific content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Employers must appoint safety managers, health managers and committees by workplace size and industry",
   "Special training required for teaching/inspection work within industrial robot operating range (Art. 36 items 31-32)",
   "Mandatory risk assessment and measures for hazardous machinery and chemicals",
   "Machinery must meet prescribed standards and safety devices must be kept effective",
   "Licensing, skills courses and plan notification for specified machinery"
  ],
